# File: tests/blender/test_clean_normals.py
# Generated from: specs/232-make-mesh-cleanup-recalculate-normals-the-way-the-geometry-normals-check-judges-them/requirements.md
Feature: Mesh cleanup leaves normals the geometry.normals check accepts

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Cleanup output never fails geometry.normals
    Given a Klein bottle with a fin that the pre-fix clean leaves with geometry.normals faces
    When clean_mesh runs on it
    Then geometry_findings reports no geometry.normals finding

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A mesh that passes validate still passes after Desktop cleanup
    Given asset "Klein" whose SM_Klein is the finned Klein bottle with no geometry findings
    When cleanup_desktop runs on "Klein"
    Then contract validate reports no geometry finding on SM_Klein

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Mobile LODs never introduce geometry.normals failures
    Given asset "Klein" after Desktop cleanup
    When optimize_mobile runs on "Klein" as a standard_prop
    Then contract validate reports no geometry.normals finding on any SM_Klein_Mobile LOD

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Faces with no consistent orientation are removed deterministically
    Given two identical copies of a closed Klein bottle whose faces stay flagged after the shared per-island recalculation
    When clean_mesh runs on each copy
    Then the flagged faces are deleted and no face is added or reshaped
    And both copies have identical vertices, faces, and normals

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Normals rule and existing clean behavior are preserved
    Given a correctly facing open quad, an inside-out closed cube, and a clean crate
    When the contract check runs on them and clean_mesh runs on the cube and the crate
    Then the quad passes and the inside-out cube is flagged before cleanup
    And the cleaned cube keeps all 6 faces facing outward with no finding
    And the cleaned crate keeps its triangle count with no geometry finding
